Z||000022||Joe Torma||09-05-2001||07:51 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by saleenfiero:<BR><B> It looks too Japanese without the back part of the roof.  It keeps reminding me of an Eclipse or something.  With the targa it rocks, but damn, that hood would cost a TON!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Agreed.  But it kinda looks goofy using the Fiero's tall B-pillars.  Maybe a notchback style.  Dunno.  I was bored and superimposed the profiles of Aus's design and a Fiero and stretched accordingly.  Too bad you'd lose the whole front fender gap thing...kinda impossible with Fiero doors.<P>Maybe Aus could make a tube frame that accepts the Fiero cradle and front suspension.  I used to build Lambos that way.<BR>I'd buy one.<P><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/simplesig.gif">  <BR>Did you get your car in my book yet????<BR> <A HREF="http://www.animatedconcepts.com/fierobook.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.animatedconcepts.com/fierobook.htm</A> ||||reg||1
